==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Linnet-Mindaugas Urbonas-3.jpg|thumb|A '''linnet''']]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|linette}}, from {{m|fro|lin||flax}}, from the bird's fondness for the seeds of flax, the source of linen.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɪnɪt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪnɪt|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[passerine]] bird, the {{vern|common linnet}} (''[[Linaria cannabina]]'', syn. ''[[Carduelis cannabina]]''), in the [[finch]] family [[Fringillidae]], native to Europe, western Asia, and north Africa.
#* '''1890''', {{w|Robert Bridges}}, ''The Shorter Poems of Robert Bridges'', Book I, V:
#*: I heard a '''linnet''' courting
#*: His lady in the spring {{...}}
# {{lb|en|US}} A [[house finch]] ({{taxlink|Haemorhous mexicanus|species|noshow=1}}), of North America.

